    },
    "body": "The fixed Dot/Lorentz/Affine adaptation study needs to compare reset lineages without weakening the existing joint comparator. Add `joint-reader-compare` for the seven sealed study evaluations: it checks the selected parent, transferred arrays, fixed 1,024-update exposure, training identity, evaluation executable/batch, and every shifted development target. It preserves paired NLL differences and original source/prose rows without an automatic quality grade or promotion.\n\nAdd optional `joint-evaluate ... --greedy-prose` for continuous Read checkpoints. It generates the five fixed greedy stories while the same model is loaded and saves a separate sealed file, preserving the existing population report and sampled outputs. Independent review corrected exclusive-writer handling and batch-shape matching. The old `joint-compare` transfer rejection remains unchanged.\n\nValidation on source `488e3976149a50dc65a9dba76735646f4ed6b8ef`: three focused release/CPU-Accelerate tests passed; three invalid CLI combinations rejected before model loading; package formatting, diff check and claim-wording check passed. The optimized test/build commands took 588.06 seconds in total. Existing unrelated warnings remain. No broad suite or repeated transfer/startup witness was run.\n\nThe prospective twelve-hour whole-study projection, build identity, review findings, resource controls and actual Dot fit launch are recorded in the evidence receipt. Dot training is in progress from frozen executable SHA256 `83984834ec014f5ea8070f9fb60e3f9f57f83ca70e97d377607c4a7d6044c08f`; Lorentz/Affine and six final evaluations remain pending. The successful greedy supplement and complete comparator have not yet been exercised on the final study artifacts. This PR delivers the study tools and launch record, not a fitted result, serving qualification or geometric-advantage claim.\n\nReferences #973 and #820.\n",
